   "subject": "How to upload ShinyApp to own host (web page)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi, i see in the documentation this:<br><br><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Source Sans Pro&#39;;font-size:14px;line-height:16px\">If you host the app at its own URL, users can visit the app (and not need to worry about code).<br></span><br>I did that, in my own webpage:<br><br><a href=\"http://omargonzalesdiaz.com/ikasa/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://omargonzalesdiaz.com/ikasa/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792400185896000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2geO13oa0vLzkyDelqfJoO\">http://omargonzalesdiaz.com/ikasa/</a><br><br>But can&#39;t access the app. I&#39;ve uploaded it to <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792400185896000&amp;usg=AOvVaw119bcjqlUPqjjmk7Op8el2\">shinyapps.io</a>,  but i want to have it in my own web page.<br><br>I can&#39;t find good documentation on doing this. May someone give my a hint? Thanks<div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-2YGcryyiqIc/VOfmjsBaBvI/AAAAAAAAAPQ/iAwZGYQChuw/s1600/omargonzales-shiny.png\" style=\"clear:left;margin-bottom:1em;float:left;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-2YGcryyiqIc/VOfmjsBaBvI/AAAAAAAAAPQ/iAwZGYQChuw/s1600/omargonzales-shiny.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792400185896000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0I4KC6fY-Okgs4GlwL_KpS\"><img src=\"https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-2YGcryyiqIc/VOfmjsBaBvI/AAAAAAAAAPQ/iAwZGYQChuw/s320/omargonzales-shiny.png\" border=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"178\"></a></p></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
